<spell-notebook "sidebar usage">
	<header level="1">
		Sidebar
		<header>A sidebar hides additional content beside a page.</>
	</>
	<sidebar-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#using-it">Using it</>
				<ui-item link="#page-structure">Page structure</>
				<ui-item link="#modal-and-persistent">Modal and persistent</>
				<ui-item link="#commands-and-events">Commands and events</>
				<ui-item link="#keyboard">Keyboard</>
				<ui-item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
				<ui-item link="#framework-usage">Framework usage</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- USAGE:  page structure, the two kinds, commands and events, keyboard, accessibility, framework snippets. -->
	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			Fomantic's three classes are three elements. `<ui-pushable>` is the clipping box (Fomantic's context); inside it,
			`<ui-sidebar>`s and one `<ui-pusher>`, the page beside them. A visible sidebar tells its pushable what it needs,
			and the pushable moves, dims or blurs the pusher.

			- `position` is the edge: `left` (default), `right`, `top`, `bottom`.
			- `width` on a side sidebar: Fomantic's words (`very thin`, `thin`, `wide`, `very wide`) or columns of the
			  viewport (`4`, `1/4`, `25%`).
			- `transition` is how it appears: `overlay`, `push`, `scale down`, `uncover` (the default at the sides; top and
			  bottom default to `overlay`), `slide along`, `slide out`.
			- `inverted` gives a dark panel: put an `inverted` menu in it.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Page structure">
		<markdown>
			For a whole page, make the pushable the viewport's height, with the sidebars and the pusher as its children.
			Fomantic's `body.pushable` and its `fixed` menus are left out on purpose: a whole-page pushable is a
			`<ui-pushable>` of viewport height, and a fixed menu goes inside the pusher.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<body>
			  <ui-pushable style="height: 100dvh">
			    <ui-sidebar id="site-menu" inverted aria-label="Site">
			      <ui-menu direction="vertical" inverted fluid aria-label="Site">
			        <ui-item link="/">Home</ui-item>
			        <ui-item link="/topics">Topics</ui-item>
			      </ui-menu>
			    </ui-sidebar>
			    <ui-pusher>
			      <ui-button commandfor="site-menu" command="--toggle" icon="sidebar">Menu</ui-button>
			      <!-- site content -->
			    </ui-pusher>
			  </ui-pushable>
			</body>
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Modal and persistent">
		<markdown>
			A sidebar is one of two things, following the WAI-ARIA patterns:

			- MODAL (the default): a drawer. A `<dialog>` that takes focus and keeps Tab inside; the pusher is dimmed and
			  inert, Escape or a click beside the sidebar closes it, and focus returns to the button that opened it.
			  `closedby` says what closes it, as on `<ui-modal>`: `any`, `closerequest` or `none`. The page doesn't
			  scroll-lock (Fomantic's `scrollLock: false`): only the pusher is blocked.
			- `persistent`: part of the page. An `<aside>` landmark (a `<ui-menu>` inside is the `<nav>`), with nothing
			  dimmed, inert or trapped, and focus left alone. Several can show at once.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Commands and events">
		<markdown>
			`visible` is the controlled state: writing it shows or hides the sidebar and fires nothing (Fomantic's `show` /
			`hide` / `toggle` behaviours).

			- User actions -- the invoker commands `--show`, `--close` and `--toggle` from a button's `commandfor`, Escape,
			  a click beside it -- dispatch the cancelable `ui-opening` / `ui-closing` first. `detail.reason` is `escape`,
			  `outside`, `close` or `close-all`.
			- `ui-opened` / `ui-closed` follow after the slide (Fomantic's `onVisible` / `onHidden`).
			- A hidden sidebar is `visibility: hidden`: out of the tab order and the accessibility tree, but still laid out.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```js
			const menu = document.querySelector("#site-menu")
			menu.addEventListener("ui-closing", (event) => {
			  if (event.detail.reason === "outside" && pinned) event.preventDefault()
			})
			menu.visible = true // show from code:  no ui-opening
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Keyboard">
		<markdown>
			| Key               | Action                                                     |
			| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
			| Tab / Shift + Tab | Move between the controls in a modal sidebar (never out)   |
			| Escape            | Close a modal sidebar (`closedby` `any` or `closerequest`) |
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- A modal sidebar is a `<dialog aria-modal="true">` (opened with `show()`, so it stays inside its pushable):
			  focus moves in, Tab stays in, the pusher is inert, and focus returns to the opener when it closes.
			- A `persistent` sidebar is an `<aside>` landmark: nothing moves focus or blocks the page.
			- Name it with `aria-label`; otherwise it is "Sidebar" (translated). Name the menu inside too.
			- Open it from a real button (`commandfor`), so keyboard and screen reader users can reach it.
			- If the element fails to render, it no longer opens or closes: it shows its children through a bare
			  `<slot>`, where they're written, with no `visible`, sliding, dimming, focus trap, Escape or events.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Framework usage">
		<markdown>Bind `visible` to your state and listen for `ui-closing` to follow the user.</>
		<header level="4" id="framework-react">React 19</>
		<markdown>
			```jsx
			<ui-sidebar visible={open} aria-label="Site" onui-close={() => setOpen(false)}>
			  ...
			</ui-sidebar>
			```
		</>
		<header level="4" id="framework-vue">Vue 3.5</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<!-- compilerOptions.isCustomElement = (tag) => tag.startsWith("ui-") -->
			<ui-sidebar :visible="open" aria-label="Site" @ui-closing="open = false">...</ui-sidebar>
			```
		</>
		<header level="4" id="framework-solid">Solid 2</>
		<markdown>
			```jsx
			// events and rich data are plain props:  `on-<event>={...}`, `options={...}`
			<ui-sidebar
			  visible={open()}
			  aria-label="Site"
			  on-ui-closing={() => setOpen(false)}
			>
			  ...
			</ui-sidebar>
			```
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
